{
  "set": "lordaeron/timber_relief",
  "rev": 1,
  "about": "The plan layer as data: for each body class, the stair core, the partitions and the furniture of every storey. Both composers (the studio's compose.mjs and the client's Compose.java) read this file; a new body size or a new room rule is a data change here. Positions are [x, z] in body coordinates (the interior is x 1..W-2, z 1..D-2, north is z 1) as integers or expressions over W, D, cx (the turned core's west column, W-4), and storeys. Each placement: { module, at, dy (layers above the storey's floor, default 1), q (quarter turns), if (an expression) }. A placement with role bed records a bed (head at `at`, foot one south); role work records the workstation (air marker for 'any', else the exact block).",
  "rules": [
    "multi-storey from 10 wide; a 7-wide body is one storey",
    "every bed a made bed: against a wall, a free long side",
    "no through rooms: every chamber opens off a landing, a passage or the hall",
    "a clear spine from the street door to the stair's foot, 2 wide at the foot",
    "furniture by use; what villagers walk to beside the spine; what nobody walks to in the corners"
  ],
  "tiles": {
    "hall": "the room the street door opens into: hearth (the west wall's middle post carries the chimney), table and benches, the workstation or a shelf by the door, stores",
    "cottage": "one room: hall and chamber together (a 5 x 5 interior can't hold two rooms 3 wide)",
    "chamber": "2 or 3 made beds against walls, a chest, a table or shelf, a lantern",
    "landing": "the 2 x 2 inside the turned core's corner, walled from the chambers, a door to each",
    "passage": "2 wide, joins a landing to chambers (13-wide bodies)"
  },
